Version 3.3

These Terms & Conditions govern your access to and use of Jericho Platform, and include the Privacy Notice at section 10. By ticking the acceptance box and completing registration, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by them. If you do not agree, do not register and do not use the Platform.

PLACEHOLDER — THIS DOCUMENT IS NOT YET COMPLETE. Some legal details, in section 16 and in the Privacy Notice at section 10, are still placeholders. They must be completed, and these Terms reviewed by a qualified lawyer, before the Platform is opened to real Participants.

1. Nature of the Platform and the role of the Operators

Jericho Platform is a private tool, provided free of charge, through which brokers, intermediaries and principals in physical commodity markets may promote and find business opportunities. The Operators act as brokers and intermediaries between Participants, and may act for both sides of the same transaction. They read what Participants send in order to protect anonymity and decide what is passed on, and they introduce counterparties to one another. This review is not a check of any Participant, offer, document or price. The Operators are intermediaries, not advisers to either party, and their only duties are those set out in these Terms. The Operators are paid for their brokerage by the commission described in section 8; the Platform itself charges nothing. The Operators broker physical commodity transactions only. The Platform is not an exchange, a clearing house, a payment service, or a broker-dealer in securities or other financial instruments. No transaction is executed, cleared, settled, financed or guaranteed through the Platform, and the Operators are never a party to any contract of sale between Participants.

2. A private, invitation-only platform

Jericho Platform is a private, invitation-only facilitation platform. It is not a public marketplace. Membership is closed: listings are not published to the public, are not indexed or advertised, and no one may join by applying. Access is granted solely at the Operators' discretion and may be suspended or revoked at any time without notice. Nothing in these Terms gives you a right to be admitted, a right to remain a Participant, or a right to be told the reason for any decision about your access.

3. Access and eligibility

Access is by invitation only and requires Operator approval. You confirm that you are acting in a professional and business capacity, that you are authorised to act for any company you represent, and that the information you provide, including the name, capacity and postal address you give when you accept these Terms, is accurate and kept up to date. If you accept these Terms as an individual, your obligations under them continue to bind you, and extend to any company or other entity you later form, control or trade through, in respect of any opportunity or introduction obtained through the Platform. You are responsible for keeping your credentials secure and for all activity carried out under your account.

4. No verification and no warranty

The Operators do not verify, endorse, or guarantee any Participant, company, listing, quantity, specification, document, certificate, price, title, or ability to perform. All information on the Platform is supplied by Participants and is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any implied warranty of accuracy, merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. The Operators do not warrant that the Platform will be uninterrupted, secure, or free from error.

5. Your own due diligence

You are solely responsible for your own due diligence and for every commercial decision you make. This includes verifying the identity, standing, and creditworthiness of any counterparty; inspecting and verifying goods, documents, and certificates; satisfying your own compliance, sanctions, and anti-money-laundering obligations; and obtaining your own independent professional advice. An introduction made by an Operator is not a recommendation and carries no assurance of any kind.

6. No professional advice

Nothing on the Platform, and nothing communicated by an Operator, constitutes financial, investment, legal, tax, accounting, or trading advice, nor an offer or solicitation to buy or sell anything. Information is provided for general business purposes only and must not be relied upon as a substitute for professional advice.

7. Anonymity and conduct

Listings are anonymous by design. You must not attempt to identify, or to cause the identification of, any other Participant, whether directly, by inference, by combining information, or by any technical means. All contact between Participants must pass through an Operator, except as section 8 allows; you must not attempt to contact another Participant directly or to circumvent the introduction process. You must not scrape, copy, resell, or redistribute content from the Platform, misrepresent yourself or the goods you offer, or use the Platform for any unlawful purpose. The answers you give when you publish a listing, including your role in the offer and what you state about its documents, are statements made by you under these Terms. You must not post false offers or demands, make false statements, or supply false, altered or forged documents, including bank documents, bills of lading, assay reports and KYC material. Doing so may lead to immediate suspension or permanent removal from the Platform, is recorded, does not cancel any commission already due, and may be reported to the relevant authorities.

8. Non-circumvention and commission

The introductions made through the Platform are the Operators' work and have commercial value. By accepting these Terms you agree that you will not bypass or circumvent the Operators, and will not attempt to conclude a transaction with any counterparty introduced to you through the Platform without the Operators' involvement. This applies to the introduced counterparty and to its affiliates, employees, agents, and related companies, and applies regardless of which side makes the approach. After an introduction, the Operators remain part of the communication between the parties until the transaction is concluded or abandoned. As the only exception, a principal may send confidential documents directly to the introduced counterparty, and to no one else; doing so is not circumvention and does not affect the Operators' commission. The commission, its basis (a percentage of the transaction value, or a fixed sum per unit in the currency of the transaction) and which party pays it are agreed in writing between the Operators and the paying party during the negotiation, before the introduction is made. You acknowledge that the Operators may act for, and receive commission from, both sides of the same transaction. The commission is payable whenever a transaction results from an introduction made through the Platform, whether that transaction is concluded directly or through any intermediary, and this obligation continues for twenty-four (24) months from the date the introduction is made. Concluding a transaction outside the Platform does not remove that entitlement.

9. Confidentiality

Information you obtain through the Platform, including listings and messages, is confidential and is made available solely for the purpose of evaluating a potential transaction. You must not disclose it to any third party, or use it for any other purpose, without the prior written consent of the Operators.

10. Privacy Notice

This section explains what personal data the Operators hold about you, why they hold it, and who can see it. It applies to everyone who registers for or uses the Platform, and forms part of these Terms.

What is collected. When you accept an invitation and register, the Platform records your first name, last name, company, job title, country, telephone number, email address, your password in securely hashed form, and your language preference. When you accept these Terms it records the name you type as your signature, whether you sign as an individual or for a company (and that company's name), and your postal address. As you use the Platform it records the listings you publish, the messages you send and receive, the document declarations you make about a listing, the searches and commodity watchlists you choose to save, the notifications generated for you, records of the emails the Platform sends you (including the recipient address, the content sent, and whether delivery succeeded), and activity records such as sign-ins, approvals, invitations, and the version and language of the Terms you accepted. The Operators also keep internal records of how each introduction progressed. These records are for the Operators' use only and are not shared with other members.

Why it is collected. This data is used to operate the Platform and for nothing else: to create and administer your account; to manage invitations and the approval of new Participants; to publish and display listings; to facilitate brokered introductions between Participants through an Operator; to communicate with you about your account and about activity relevant to you; to keep the Platform secure and to detect misuse; and to maintain an audit trail of what was done, by whom, and when.

Who can see it. Your identity and contact details are visible only to the Operators. Participants never see one another's identity: listings are published anonymously, and every message between Participants passes through an Operator, who decides what is passed on. No other Participant is shown your name, company, country, telephone number, or email address through the Platform. There is one exception, and it only happens with your agreement. Where the Operators consider that two Participants should deal with one another, they will ask each of you separately whether you agree to be introduced. If, and only if, both of you agree, the Operators will disclose each party's identity and contact details to the other so that you can deal directly. That introduction is made by email, outside the Platform. You are always asked first and you may decline, and until you agree the anonymity described above continues to apply.

Your data is not sold, rented, or traded, and it is not shared with third parties for their own purposes. It is disclosed only to the service providers used to run the Platform itself - hosting, database, and email delivery, named in the next paragraph - which act on the Operators' instructions, and where the Operators are required to disclose it by law or need to do so to establish, exercise, or defend a legal claim.

Where your data is processed. The Platform runs on services provided by third parties, which act only on instructions given by the Operators: Supabase provides the database and the authentication system, Resend delivers the email the Platform sends, and GitHub Actions runs its scheduled tasks. The database is hosted in [PLACEHOLDER — database hosting region]. Email delivery and the scheduled tasks are carried out by providers established in the United States, so where the Platform emails you, your email address and the content of that message are transferred outside the United Kingdom and the European Economic Area. The safeguard relied on for that transfer is [PLACEHOLDER — international transfer safeguard, for example UK IDTA or EU Standard Contractual Clauses]. You may ask the Operators for details of these arrangements using the contact address below.

How long it is kept. Data is retained only for as long as it is needed to operate the Platform and to protect the Operators' legal position, after which it is deleted or anonymised. Records that exist to evidence what was agreed - your acceptance of these Terms, with a copy of the details you gave when accepting them, and the audit trail of introductions made - are kept for as long as a claim arising from them could still be brought, including after your membership ends or your account is deleted.

Operator access. The Operators may access all data held on the Platform, including listings, messages, and account details, for the purposes of brokerage and of security. This is inherent in how the Platform works: an Operator cannot introduce two Participants, or keep them anonymous to one another, without seeing what both have published and written.

Data controller. The controller responsible for your personal data is Rafael Efraim, of [PLACEHOLDER — data controller registered address]. Questions about your data, and requests to access, correct, or delete it, should be sent to rafael@myplatform.trade.

Complaints. If you believe your personal data has not been handled properly, you may raise it with the Operators using the contact details above, and you may complain to the competent supervisory authority, [PLACEHOLDER — competent data protection supervisory authority], at [PLACEHOLDER — supervisory authority address and contact details].

11. Limitation of liability

To the fullest extent permitted by law, neither the Platform nor the Operators are liable for any loss or damage of any kind arising out of or in connection with your use of the Platform or with any dealing between Participants. This includes, without limitation, financial loss, loss of profit, loss of opportunity, loss of goodwill, business interruption, loss arising from a transaction that does not complete or completes on unfavourable terms, and loss caused by the act, omission, misrepresentation, default, insolvency, or fraud of any Participant or third party. The Operators are not liable for any indirect or consequential loss. Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits any liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, including liability for fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence.

12. Disputes between Participants

Any dispute between Participants is solely a matter between those Participants. The Operators are not a party to it, are under no obligation to investigate, mediate, arbitrate, or resolve it, and accept no responsibility for its outcome. You release the Operators from all claims arising out of any such dispute.

13. Suspension and withdrawal of access

The Operators may suspend, restrict, or withdraw your access to the Platform at any time, at their sole discretion, with or without notice and without being required to give reasons, including where they consider that these Terms have been breached or that continued access presents a risk to other Participants. Access to the Platform is a privilege and not a right, and confers no ownership interest or entitlement.

14. Changes to these Terms

The Operators may amend these Terms from time to time. Where an amendment is material, you will be asked to accept the updated version before continuing to use the Platform. Your continued use of the Platform after an amendment takes effect constitutes acceptance of it.

15. Governing law, courts and service

These Terms, and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with them, shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the law of England and Wales. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with these Terms, including any question regarding their existence, validity or termination, shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Courts of the Dubai International Financial Centre. By accepting these Terms you expressly agree in writing to that jurisdiction, as a specific, clear and express agreement under Article 14(B) of Dubai Law No. (2) of 2025. You agree that any claim or court document may be served on you by email to the address registered to your account, and at the postal address you gave when accepting these Terms, or any later address you give the Operators in writing.

16. The Operators: company details and notices

The Platform is operated by Rafael Efraim ("the Operators"), an independent broker trading under his own name until the operating company is incorporated. The company will be incorporated in [PLACEHOLDER — country of incorporation] under company registration number [PLACEHOLDER — company registration number].

Registered office: [PLACEHOLDER — registered office address].

Trading address, where different from the registered office: [PLACEHOLDER — trading address].

VAT or tax registration number: [PLACEHOLDER — VAT or tax registration number].

Notices under these Terms must be given in writing to rafael@myplatform.trade and to the registered office above, and take effect on receipt.

